---
// The hero's only decorative flourish — a bigger, more saturated multi-stop
// bloom built from DESIGN.md's develop/preview/ship gradient stops, sized to
// the hero itself so it reads as a full mesh rather than a floating blob,
// with a soft fade at the bottom into the section border. Nowhere else on
// the site uses color at this intensity; everything else stays ink-on-canvas.
---

<div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 -z-10 overflow-hidden" aria-hidden="true">
	<div
		class="absolute inset-0 opacity-[0.5] blur-[70px]"
		style="background: radial-gradient(38% 55% at 12% 15%, #007cf0, transparent),
			radial-gradient(34% 48% at 85% 8%, #7928ca, transparent),
			radial-gradient(42% 58% at 55% 58%, #50e3c2, transparent),
			radial-gradient(36% 50% at 92% 70%, #ff4d4d, transparent),
			radial-gradient(32% 46% at 4% 75%, #007cf0, transparent);"
	>
	</div>
	<div class="absolute inset-x-0 bottom-0 h-32" style="background: linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent, var(--color-canvas));"></div>
</div>
